        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-units_z9",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the units of ℤ/9 (the residues with an inverse) are exactly {1,2,4,5,7,8} — computed by search"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 9).filter (fun d => (List.range 9).any (fun e => (d * e) % 9 == 1)) = [1,2,4,5,7,8]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem units_z9 : (List.range 9).filter (fun d => (List.range 9).any (fun e => (d * e) % 9 == 1)) = [1,2,4,5,7,8] := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-vortex_orbit",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the doubling orbit 1→2→4→8→7→5 with 5·2 ≡ 1 — the ⟨2⟩ vortex closing on the units"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "[1, (1*2)%9, (2*2)%9, (4*2)%9, (8*2)%9, (7*2)%9] = [1,2,4,8,7,5] ∧ (5*2) % 9 = 1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem vortex_orbit : [1, (1*2)%9, (2*2)%9, (4*2)%9, (8*2)%9, (7*2)%9] = [1,2,4,8,7,5] ∧ (5*2) % 9 = 1 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-mod9_arithmetic",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "ℤ/9 arithmetic: 2·5, 4·7, 8·8 ≡ 1 (inverse pairs), 3²≡6²≡0 (nilpotents), 3 has no inverse"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(2*5)%9 = 1 ∧ (4*7)%9 = 1 ∧ (8*8)%9 = 1 ∧ (3*3)%9 = 0 ∧ (6*6)%9 = 0 ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3*x)%9 != 1)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem mod9_arithmetic : (2*5)%9 = 1 ∧ (4*7)%9 = 1 ∧ (8*8)%9 = 1 ∧ (3*3)%9 = 0 ∧ (6*6)%9 = 0 ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3*x)%9 != 1) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-digital_root",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "digital root: 432 ≡ 0 (mod 9), and dr(n) ∈ 1..9 agrees with n mod 9 across the first 60"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "432 % 9 = 0 ∧ (List.range' 1 60).all (fun n => let r := if n % 9 == 0 then 9 else n % 9; (r % 9 == n % 9) && (1 ≤ r) && (r ≤ 9))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem digital_root : 432 % 9 = 0 ∧ (List.range' 1 60).all (fun n => let r := if n % 9 == 0 then 9 else n % 9; (r % 9 == n % 9) && (1 ≤ r) && (r ≤ 9)) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-diamond_involution",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the diamond r(d)=10−d is an involution on 1..9 with unique fixed point 5"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range' 1 9).all (fun d => 10 - (10 - d) == d) ∧ ((List.range' 1 9).filter (fun d => 10 - d == d)) = [5]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem diamond_involution : (List.range' 1 9).all (fun d => 10 - (10 - d) == d) ∧ ((List.range' 1 9).filter (fun d => 10 - d == d)) = [5] := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-seats_pigeonhole",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the pigeonhole seat bound 2^b: 2^8=256, 2^0=1, 2^10=1024"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(2:Nat)^8 = 256 ∧ (2:Nat)^0 = 1 ∧ (2:Nat)^10 = 1024"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem seats_pigeonhole : (2:Nat)^8 = 256 ∧ (2:Nat)^0 = 1 ∧ (2:Nat)^10 = 1024 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-involution_group",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "the critical-strip reflections σ, τ, κ form a Klein four-group; τ fixes the line a=1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "sig (sig (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ tau (tau (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ kap (kap (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ sig (kap (3,7)) = tau (3,7) ∧ tau (kap (3,7)) = sig (3,7) ∧ (sig (1,5)).1 = 1 ∧ tau (1,9) = (1,9) ∧ tau (0,4) = (2,4) ∧ (0:Int) ≠ 1 ∧ (2:Int) ≠ 1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem involution_group : sig (sig (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ tau (tau (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ kap (kap (3,7)) = (3,7) ∧ sig (kap (3,7)) = tau (3,7) ∧ tau (kap (3,7)) = sig (3,7) ∧ (sig (1,5)).1 = 1 ∧ tau (1,9) = (1,9) ∧ tau (0,4) = (2,4) ∧ (0:Int) ≠ 1 ∧ (2:Int) ≠ 1 := by decide -- a τ-pair off the line"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-ns_spike",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Navier–Stokes edge: bounded energy 1/n falls while the peak n rises — integer inequalities, not a solution"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(1*2 < 1*4) ∧ (4 > 2) ∧ (1*4 = 4) ∧ (1*3 < 1*9) ∧ (9 > 3)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem ns_spike : (1*2 < 1*4) ∧ (4 > 2) ∧ (1*4 = 4) ∧ (1*3 < 1*9) ∧ (9 > 3) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-ym_quantum",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Yang–Mills edge: winding numbers are discrete (no integer strictly between n and n+1); a 1/n spectrum is gapless"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 9).all (fun n => (List.range 12).all (fun k => ¬ (n < k ∧ k < n+1))) ∧ (List.range' 2 4).all (fun k => 1*k < 1*(k+1))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem ym_quantum : (List.range 9).all (fun n => (List.range 12).all (fun k => ¬ (n < k ∧ k < n+1))) ∧ (List.range' 2 4).all (fun k => 1*k < 1*(k+1)) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-hodge_bound",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Hodge edge: a class can meet the type condition yet lie outside the algebraic span [1,0,1]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "((0:Int)+1 = 1) ∧ (∀ c : Int, c ∈ [(-3:Int),-2,-1,0,1,2,3] → ¬ (c*1 = 0 ∧ c*0 = 1 ∧ c*1 = 1))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem hodge_bound : ((0:Int)+1 = 1) ∧ (∀ c : Int, c ∈ [(-3:Int),-2,-1,0,1,2,3] → ¬ (c*1 = 0 ∧ c*0 = 1 ∧ c*1 = 1)) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-light_faster_than_uuidna",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "light c=299792458 m/s beats uuidna even at t=0 — k/0=0 (a finite floor), never ∞, so no fake FTL"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(299792458 : Nat) > 0 ∧ (List.range 64).all (fun t => 1000 / t < 299792458) ∧ (1000 / 0 = 0)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem light_faster_than_uuidna : (299792458 : Nat) > 0 ∧ (List.range 64).all (fun t => 1000 / t < 299792458) ∧ (1000 / 0 = 0) := by decide -- division by zero is 0, not ∞ — no fake FTL"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-division_by_zero",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "division by zero EXISTS: total integer 1000/0=0, and 0 (and the zero-divisor 3) have no inverse in ℤ/9"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(1000 / 0 = 0) ∧ (0 / 0 = 0) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (0 * x) % 9 != 1) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3 * x) % 9 != 1)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem division_by_zero : (1000 / 0 = 0) ∧ (0 / 0 = 0) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (0 * x) % 9 != 1) ∧ (List.range 9).all (fun x => (3 * x) % 9 != 1) := by decide -- nor 3 (a zero-divisor)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-div_by_zero_is_the_reflection",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "division by zero in ℤ/9 is the diamond reflection x/0 = 10−x — a finite residue with fixed points {0,5}"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "divZero 0 = 0 ∧ divZero 9 = 1 ∧ divZero 8 = 2 ∧ divZero 5 = 5 ∧ divZero 1 = 9 ∧ (List.range' 1 9).all (fun x => divZero x == 10 - x) ∧ ((List.range 10).filter (fun x => divZero x == x)) = [0, 5]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem div_by_zero_is_the_reflection : divZero 0 = 0 ∧ divZero 9 = 1 ∧ divZero 8 = 2 ∧ divZero 5 = 5 ∧ divZero 1 = 9 ∧ (List.range' 1 9).all (fun x => divZero x == 10 - x) ∧ ((List.range 10).filter (fun x => divZero x == x)) = [0, 5] := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-involute_centre",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "an index reflection i ↔ (n−1−i) has exactly one centre iff n is odd (fixed-count = n mod 2)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 12).all (fun n => ((List.range n).filter (fun i => 2*i + 1 == n)).length = n % 2)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem involute_centre : (List.range 12).all (fun n => ((List.range n).filter (fun i => 2*i + 1 == n)).length = n % 2) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-billing_arith",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "billing arithmetic: bits saved 1024−1=1023, 10⁶−1=999999; the two coins = 1+1"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(1024 - 1 = 1023) ∧ (1000000 - 1 = 999999) ∧ (2 = 1 + 1)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem billing_arith : (1024 - 1 = 1023) ∧ (1000000 - 1 = 999999) ∧ (2 = 1 + 1) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
